 "notes": "The Cargill salt-loading pier: the conveyor trestle on rows of sponge-covered concrete pillars from the shore to the pier head, the berth with its mooring dolphins, sandy shallows at 3-8 m and the natural reef sloping from about 15 m to 30 m beyond the pier (bonaire.com, scubadiving.com). Pier geometry from OpenStreetMap; the pillar rows are drawn as two lines either side of the conveyor because the individual pillar positions are not published, and the 30 m contour and the route are estimates. Diving is only allowed when no ship is loading. Coastline, pier and dive-site markers © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
